      "summary": "Sansa made of wood with flaring ends and curved base. Sansa has twelve iron tongues secured by single iron rod bound with metal loops which pass through the instrument. Lateral wood rod supports tongues above, curved iron bar supports tongues below. Glass beads - three large white, one large blue and one small red - set into resin above the tongues. Further three large white glass beads and one small red bead set into resin at lower end of sansa. Band of resin across back of sansa has three white glass beads, one red, one blue and one half black glass bead set into it. Twisted metal rod at lower end of sansa has tubular iron rattle attached.",
